hadiths[500]{hadithnumber,text}:
1,"Ahmad ibn Abd al-Qahir ibn al-Anbari al-Lakhmi al-Dimashqi, resident of Damascus in the year 279 AH, narrated to us: Mubashshir ibn Uthman narrated to us: Sadaqah ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: al-Wadin ibn Ata narrated to us: from Mahfuz ibn Alqamah: from Abd al-Rahman ibn A'id al-Azdi: from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""The noblest part of faith is that people feel safe from you; the noblest part of Islam is that people are safe from your tongue and hand; the noblest part of hijrah is that you abandon sins; and the noblest part of jihad is that you kill and hamstring your horse."" No one narrated it from al-Wadin except Sadaqah; Mubashshir ibn Uthman narrated it uniquely."
2,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 2 Arabic Hadees: 13
3,"Abu al-Dahdah Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Udhri al-Dimashqi narrated to us in Damascus; Musa ibn Amir Abu Amir narrated to us; al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us; Khulayd ibn Da'lij narrated to us; Abu Ghalib narrated to us, saying:The heads of the Kharijites were brought and erected on the steps of the Mosque of Damascus. People began looking at them, and I went out to look at them. Then Abu Umamah arrived, riding a donkey and wearing a Sunbulani shirt. He looked at them and said: ""What has Satan done to this nation?"" — saying it three times — ""The worst of those killed under the shade of heaven are these. The best of those killed under the shade of heaven are those killed by these. These are the dogs of Hellfire"" — saying it three times. Then he wept and turned away.Abu Ghalib said: I followed him and said: ""I heard you say something just now; did you say it yourself?"" He said: ""Glory be to Allah! If so, I would be bold. Rather, I heard that from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ many times."" I said to him: ""I saw you weep."" He said: ""Out of mercy for them; they were once from the people of Islam."" Then he said to me: ""Do you not recite?"" I said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Then recite from Surah Ali Imran."" I recited. He said: ""Do you not hear the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: 'As for those in whose hearts is deviation, they follow that which is ambiguous of it' (Surah Ali Imran, 3:7)? There was deviation in the hearts of these, so they were caused to deviate. Recite at the hundredth verse."" I recited until I reached: ""On the Day when faces will turn white and faces will turn black. As for those whose faces turn black: 'Did you disbelieve after your belief?'"" (Surah Ali Imran, 3:106). I said: ""O Abu Umamah, are they these?"" He said: ""Yes, they are these.""No one narrated it from Khulayd ibn Da'lij except Ibn al-Walid."
4,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 4 Arabic Hadees: 59
5,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 5 Arabic Hadees: 67
6,"Ahmed bin Al-Husayn bin Mabihran, Abu Abdillah Al-Idaji, narrated to us; Muhammad bin Marzuq Al-Basri narrated to us; Hani' bin Yahya Al-Sulami narrated to us; Al-Hasan bin Ja'far Al-Jafri narrated to us; from Qatadah; from Yahya bin Waththab; from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When Allah spoke to Musa, he could perceive the crawling of ants upon the smooth rock on a pitch-black night from a distance of ten farsakhs."" No one narrated it from Qatadah except Al-Hasan bin Ja'far, and Hani' bin Yahya was the sole narrator of this chain."
7,"Aḥmad ibn ʿImrān Abū Mūsā al-Sūsī narrated to us in Baghdad; Abū al-Rabīʿ ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥārithī narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Sufyān ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Rawāḥah al-Baṣrī narrated to us; from Sulaymān al-Taymī; from Abū ʿUthmān al-Nahdī; from Salmān al-Fārisī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""There is a sin that is not forgiven, a sin that is not overlooked, and a sin that is forgiven. As for the sin that is not forgiven, it is associating partners with Allah (shirk). As for the sin that is not overlooked, it is the oppression of servants against one another. As for the sin that is forgiven, it is the sin of the servant between him and Allah the Exalted."" No one narrated it from Sulaymān al-Taymī except Yazīd ibn Sufyān; Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated it uniquely."
8,"Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Naṣr al-Ḥazzā' al-Baghdādī narrated to us; Shabāb al-'Uṣfurī narrated to us; Unays ibn Sawwār al-Jarmī narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Mālik ibn al-Ḥuwayrith narrated to us, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When Allah, glorified be His mention, intends to create a human being, and a man has intercourse with a woman, his fluid flows into every vein and nerve of hers. Then, when the seventh day arrives, Allah brings forth for him every vein between him and Adam. Then he recited: 'In whatever form He willed, He assembled you' (Sūrat al-Infiṭār, verse 8).""This is not narrated from Mālik ibn al-ḥuwayrith except through this chain; Ibn Sawwār narrated it exclusively."
9,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 9 Arabic Hadees: 112
10,"Ahmed ibn Umar ibn Shurayh al-Qadi Abu al-Abbas narrated to us: Al-Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim narrated to us: Surah ibn al-Hakam al-Qadi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to us: from al-Sha'bi: from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa: from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Three will be given their rewards twice: a man from the People of the Book who believed in his prophet, then lived to see the Prophet (peace be upon him) and believed in him; a man who had a slave-girl, freed her, then married her; and a slave who feared Allah and obeyed his masters."" It was not narrated from Ibn Habib except by Sawdah; Al-Abbas ibn Muhammad narrated it uniquely."
11,"Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn 'Anbar al-Basri narrated to us; Musa ibn Maymun ibn Musa al-Mar'i narrated to us; my father narrated to us; from his father; from his grandfather 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Safwan ibn Qudamah, who said: My father Safwan emigrated to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and pledged allegiance to him for Islam. The Prophet (peace be upon him) extended his hand and wiped over it. Safwan said: ""I love you, O Messenger of Allah."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said to him: ""A person is with whom he loves."" This is not narrated from Safwan ibn Qudamah except through this chain; Ibn Maymun narrated it uniquely."
12,"Ahmad ibn Isma'il al-Wasawini al-Basri narrated to us: Shiban ibn Farrukh narrated to us: al-Sa'q ibn Hazn al-Qaysi narrated to us: Matar al-Warraq narrated to us: Zuhdam al-Jarmi narrated to us, saying: I entered upon Abu Musa al-Ash'ari while he was eating chicken meat. He said: ""Come and eat."" I said: ""I have sworn not to eat chicken meat."" Abu Musa said: ""Eat, for I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) eating from it. And I will inform you about your oath. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I and my companions, and some companions of mine, seeking mounts from him. He swore that he would not give us mounts, and he had no mounts available. By Allah, we had not left until some young, white-crested female camels came to him. He ordered mounts for us. When we left, we remembered the oath of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so we returned to him. He said: 'What brought you back?' We said: 'We remembered your oath, O Messenger of Allah, and we feared that you might have forgotten it.' He said (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): 'By Allah, I did not forget it, but whoever swears an oath, then sees something better than it, let him do that which is better, and let him expiate his oath.'"" No one narrated it from Matar except al-Sa'q."
13,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 13 Arabic Hadees: 154
14,"Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Khuzāʿī al-Iṣbahānī Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us; Sahl ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAskarī narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn Thābit narrated to us; from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid; from Qays ibn Abī Ḥāzim, who said: I heard Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, may Allah be pleased with him, while he was on the pulpit, saying: ""The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, stood in this place of mine in the first year, and said: 'No one has been given anything after certainty like well-being, and we ask Allah for well-being in this world and the Hereafter. Behold, verily truthfulness and righteousness are in Paradise. Behold, verily lying and wickedness are in the Fire.'"" No one narrated it from Ismāʿīl except ʿAmr ibn Thābit ibn Abī al-Miqdām; Sahl ibn Muḥammad narrated it uniquely."
15,"Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Ansari, Abu Ja'far al-Asbahani, narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn Yusuf ibn Qutayba al-Hamdani narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn Adi, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) said: ""Three are from the character of faith: whoever, when angry, does not let his anger lead him into falsehood; and whoever, when pleased, does not let his pleasure take him out of a right; and whoever, when he has power, does not seize what is not his."" No one narrated it from al-Zubayr ibn Adi except Bishr ibn al-Husayn."
16,"Khalifah ibn Muhammad al-Mawsili narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn 'Arafah narrated to us; Musa ibn Mas'ud Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us; al-Haytham ibn al-Jahm al-Mu'adhdhin narrated to us, from 'Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Verily, when the drop (nutfah) settles in the womb, it remains a drop for forty nights, then it becomes a clot (alaqah) for forty nights, then it becomes a lump of flesh (mudghah) for forty nights, then it becomes bones for forty nights, then Allah clothes the bones with flesh. Then the angel says: 'O Lord, male or female?' So Allah the Mighty and Majestic decrees, and the angel writes. Then he says: 'O Lord, wretched or fortunate?' So Allah the Mighty and Majestic decrees, and the angel writes. Then he says: 'O Lord, his lifespan, his provision, and his traces?' So Allah the Mighty and Majestic decrees, and the angel writes."" No one narrated it from 'Asim except al-Haytham ibn al-Jahm, Abu 'Uthman ibn al-Haytham, and no one narrated it from him except Abu Hudhayfah. Al-Hasan ibn 'Arafah narrated it uniquely."
17,"Abd Allah ibn al-Ṣaqr al-Sukkarī al-Baghdādī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Muṣaffā narrated to us: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walīd narrated to us: from al-Awzāʿī: from Ibn Jurayj: from Abū al-Zubayr: from Jābir (may Allah be pleased with him): from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family), who said: ""The Magians of this Ummah are those who deny the divine decrees of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic. If they fall ill, do not visit them; if you meet them, do not greet them; and if they die, do not attend their funerals."" No one narrated it from al-Awzāʿī except Baqiyyah; Ibn Muṣaffā narrated it uniquely."
18,"Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn al-Sabbah al-Saffar al-Isbahani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Furat al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Abdawih al-Sindi al-Razi narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Muttarif ibn Tarif, from al-Minhal ibn Amr al-Tamimi, from Ibn Abbas, who said: ""We used to discuss that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and his family and grant them peace, entrusted seventy trusts to Ali which he did not entrust to anyone else."" No one narrated it from Muttarif except Amr ibn Qays, and no one narrated it from Amr except Sahl, and Ahmad ibn al-Furat was unique in narrating it. The name of al-Tamimi is Arbadah."
19,"Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab al-Manatiqi al-Ramli narrated to us: Muhammad bin Ismail al-Sayigh narrated to us: Ubaydullah bin Sufyan al-Ghadani narrated to us: from Ibn Awn, from Zayd bin Wahb, from Abdullah bin Mas'ud: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) narrated to us, and he is the truthful, the believed: ""Verily, the creation of one of you is gathered in his mother's womb for forty days, then it becomes a clot (ʿalaqah) like that, then it becomes a lump of flesh (muḍghah) like that, then the angel comes and writes: wretched or fortunate, male or female."" No one narrated it from Ibn Awn except Ubaydullah bin Sufyan."
20,"Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub al-Ansari al-Baghdadi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Unaysi, Abu Abd Allah, narrated to us; Isma ibn Muhammad al-Ansari narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Indeed, 'Al-Salam' (Peace) is a name from the names of Allah the Exalted, which He placed upon the earth as a greeting for the people of our religion, and a security for the people of our covenant (dhimmis)."" No one narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'id except Isma ibn Muhammad; Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Unaysi narrated it uniquely, who is from the descendants of Abd Allah ibn Unays al-Ansari."
21,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 21 Arabic Hadees: 338
22,"Al-Ḥasan ibn Ḥubāsh al-Ḥimmānī al-Kūfī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-ʿAṭṭār al-Kūfī narrated to us; Sayf ibn ʿAmīrah narrated to us; from Abān ibn Taghlib; Simāk ibn Ḥarb narrated to us; from Shahr ibn Ḥawshab; from Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man asked him, saying: ""I speak to myself about something that if I were to utter it, it would invalidate my reward."" He said: ""None encounters that speech except a believer."" No one narrated it from Abān ibn Taghlib except Sayf ibn ʿAmīrah, and it is not narrated from Umm Salamah except through this chain."
23,"Al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad ibn Fāhid al-Narsī al-Baghdādī narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿīd al-Jawharī narrated to us; Abū Aḥmad al-Zubayrī narrated to us; Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated to us, from Ayyūb and Ismāʿīl ibn Ummayyah, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""These are for this, and these are for this,"" whereupon the people dispersed while they did not differ concerning the Divine Decree (al-Qadar).No one narrated it from Sufyān except Abū Aḥmad al-Zubayrī; Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿīd al-Jawharī alone narrated it; and no one narrated it from Ayyūb and Ismāʿīl ibn Ummayyah except Sufyān.Some scholars said: ""This Ayyūb from whom Sufyān narrated this hadith is Ayyūb ibn Mūsā."" Others said: ""He is Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī,"" and this is the correct view in my opinion, because if he were Ayyūb ibn Mūsā he would not have narrated from him at all without attribution; but due to the eminence of Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī he did not attribute him."
24,"Al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim al-'Ijli narrated to us: Al-Husayn ibn 'Ali ibn Yazid al-Sudai narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Hafs al-Ghadiri narrated to us: From Musa al-Saghir: From 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Utbah: From Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever says 'There is no god but Allah,' it will benefit him one day of his time, even if it is after the punishment afflicts him."" No one narrated it from Musa al-Saghir except Hafs al-Ghadiri, and Al-Husayn ibn 'Ali al-Sudai narrated it uniquely from his father."
25,"Khalaf ibn al-Hasan al-Wasiti narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Shami narrated to us: Sawd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""The destruction of my Ummah lies in three things: in the Qadariyyah (those who deny divine decree), in 'asabiyyah (tribalism/partisanship), and in narrating from other than a reliable, established narrator."" No one narrated it from al-Awza'i except Sawd. Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated it uniquely. Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Shami, similarly."
26,Al-Mu'jam al-Saghir Tabarani Hadees: 26 Arabic Hadees: 443
